WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:07.120
The third coronavirus stimulus package has now&nbsp;
passed the House and Senate of the United States,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.080
slightly different versions were passed,&nbsp;
meaning it will go back to the House for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:19.040
expected signature tomorrow. But most notably, the&nbsp;
third coronavirus stimulus package passed the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:27.840
Senate with zero Republican support. Not a single&nbsp;
Republican senator voted for getting money to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:36.320
more than 80 percent of Americans and getting them&nbsp;
some stimulus during this once every hundred year&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:42.560
pandemic situation that we currently are&nbsp;
facing. Let's look at Senator Patrick Leahy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:49.120
announcing the passage of the bill in the Senate&nbsp;
to Democratic applause and I would say Republicans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:54.560
silence. It actually looks like Republican&nbsp;
absence altogether. Take a look at this. Oh, no.

00:00:54.560 --> 00:01:11.840
Senator wishes change a vote, if not the year&nbsp;
or 50 days of 49 bill as amended is passed.

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:27.680
Now, there are many, many things to talk about&nbsp;
here, first of all, because the Senate passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.680 --> 00:01:33.200
a different version than the House, like I said.&nbsp;
The bill now goes back to the House and the House&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:39.680
is expected to pass this tomorrow, Tuesday. Then&nbsp;
it will go to Joe Biden for signature. And then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:44.160
soon we will see money start to go out.&nbsp;
Could be within a week, could be 10 days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:48.080
could be a little longer. Now, the bill is&nbsp;
one point nine dollars billion in total.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:54.800
It includes fourteen hundred dollar stimulus&nbsp;
checks for those making up to seventy five&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:02:00.240
thousand dollars a year. It phases out to&nbsp;
zero at eighty thousand dollars a year, three&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:08.080
hundred dollars per week in enhanced unemployment&nbsp;
benefits through summer, a child tax allowance of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:12.960
up to 3600 dollars for one year. That that's&nbsp;
actually really big. And that's something that

00:02:12.960 --> 00:02:16.560
here is being done on a temporary basis. But&nbsp;
there are many Democrats who would like to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:23.600
the tax code benefit parents through making such&nbsp;
allowances permanent. And that's something that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:26.560
can talk about as well. The bill includes&nbsp;
three hundred and fifty billion dollars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:32.240
for state coronavirus aid, 34 billion&nbsp;
dollars to expand Obamacare subsidies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.240
and 14 billion dollars for vaccine distribution.&nbsp;
Now, if you have kids, this is a big win for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:43.280
you. You would still get the 14 hundred dollar&nbsp;
stimulus check for each child and for yourself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.840
Plus, the tax credit is going up to the&nbsp;
thirty six hundred or three thousand if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:56.720
the child is six and older. And there is really a&nbsp;
lot here for families with kids. And yet the bill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:03.760
passed 50 to 49. The reason it's 50 to 49 is one&nbsp;
Republican senator was missing because of a family

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:09.440
emergency. Had he been there, it would have been&nbsp;
a 50/50 tie and then Kamala Harris would have had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:14.880
to come in and vote to break that tie. Kamala&nbsp;
Harris didn't need to come in to break the tie.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.880 --> 00:03:22.080
All 50 Democrats voted yes. All 49 Republicans&nbsp;
who voted voted no. And this gets into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:29.520
discussions about the political process that went&nbsp;
into getting us to where we are today. There are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:36.320
people rightly frustrated by the watering&nbsp;
down of this bill by Democrats, but there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:42.400
are also people reacting to this stimulus saga by&nbsp;
saying Democrats and Republicans are the same and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:47.920
they're equally worthless when it comes to getting&nbsp;
people money that they need. The first take seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:54.960
correct to me. The second take is invariably&nbsp;
wrong, unquestionably wrong. I share your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.960 --> 00:04:01.040
frustration and believe it's terrible that Biden&nbsp;
said this would happen right away, but it actually

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:06.640
will be close to April before people see money.&nbsp;
I understood two thousand dollars to mean two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:12.240
thousand more dollars, not 4500 more, which&nbsp;
makes it two thousand total if you include&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.240 --> 00:04:16.800
the 600 dollars that will have been six months&nbsp;
before by the time people actually start getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.920
the fourteen hundred. Yeah, I'm with you right&nbsp;
there. I hate that the 15 dollar minimum wage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:27.600
was removed from the bill. I hate that the bill&nbsp;
further restricted thanks to Senate Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.920
who qualifies at all for the stimulus, reducing it&nbsp;
from one hundred thousand a year to 80000 a year.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:37.680
This shows us some terrible realities&nbsp;
about the Democratic Party, including&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:42.080
that the most centrist of the Senate Democrats,&nbsp;
people like Joe Manchin and Jeanne Shaheen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.840
they are very soft Democrats. They're obviously&nbsp;
not progressives. And while they are Democrats,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.880
they're not Republicans. They are&nbsp;
Democrats. They're very different

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.600
than what you and I might say is the type&nbsp;
of Democrat that we want to see in the U.S.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.600 --> 00:05:00.000
Senate. But it's important to remember for those&nbsp;
like there's people mad at the parliamentarian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.480
because the parliamentarian said you can't&nbsp;
include the 15 dollar minimum wage in the bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:09.600
but Kamala Harris could have done an override.&nbsp;
Remember that even if Kamala Harris overrules&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.400
the Senate parliamentarian and says we are&nbsp;
putting the 15 dollar minimum wage in the bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:20.640
then you look at the mansion vote and likely&nbsp;
some others, and you don't even pass the bill&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.640 --> 00:05:26.240
at all and no one gets money. So there is a huge&nbsp;
critique of the Democratic Party to be made here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.240 --> 00:05:30.080
and it should be made. And we've been making&nbsp;
it, which is that lots of these Democrats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:35.520
aren't very progressive at all. At the&nbsp;
same time, the overruling on fifteen

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.240
dollars minimum wage just means it doesn't pass&nbsp;
at all. And I don't think that's good either.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:44.720
Now, on the other hand, every Republican&nbsp;
senator voted for people to get&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:51.200
zero and look at what still Democrats were able&nbsp;
to get done. So this is the other perspective.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.200 --> 00:05:56.800
Republican Senator Ron Johnson for no reason other&nbsp;
than to try to delay the bill, although it failed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:03.280
Ask that the entire bill be read aloud.&nbsp;
Republicans have acted to get people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:10.960
zero and to make it take as long as possible to&nbsp;
give them zero. And despite that, Democrats have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.200
have been able to pass. And when the House&nbsp;
votes for the updated version of the bill,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:22.480
they will pass a nearly two trillion dollar. That&nbsp;
puts thousands of dollars into the bank accounts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:28.080
of the typical family of four between the stimulus&nbsp;
money and the child credit. It establishes the

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:33.920
country's first real child allowance. It's only&nbsp;
on a temporary basis for now, but there's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:39.360
possibility it could be made permanent, which it&nbsp;
should be. This is obviously nowhere close to what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:45.760
the American people deserve, but it's important to&nbsp;
resist the urge to self righteously slam it all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:49.600
write it off and say Democrats&nbsp;
and Republicans are the same.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.600 --> 00:06:54.560
This is a major legislative accomplishment&nbsp;
and it's desperately needed by Joe Biden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:59.600
It's not what was promised and it took way too&nbsp;
long. And those are critiques that are fair.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.600 --> 00:07:04.960
So when we equate Republicans and Democrats here,&nbsp;
it's silly. Although there are many criticisms&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.960 --> 00:07:08.720
to be made of Democrats, their positions&nbsp;
aren't even remotely comparable, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:14.960
morally and legislatively to those of Republicans.&nbsp;
Now, if you were going to claim that this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.920
merely happening, Democrats vote yes, Republicans&nbsp;
vote no because Joe Biden is president. And

00:07:19.920 --> 00:07:23.600
if things were reversed and it was a Republican&nbsp;
president, you would have the reverse situation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:29.120
The answer is obviously not. Democrats voted&nbsp;
for every coronavirus relief bill during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.120 --> 00:07:35.200
Trump administration. Not a single Republican&nbsp;
voted for Joe Biden's covid relief bill. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:39.120
yet you still have Republicans lecturing&nbsp;
Democrats about the need for unity and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:44.000
bipartisanship. And we're supposed to pretend&nbsp;
both parties are the same. So give me a come on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:49.920
guys. You've got to give me a break on that.&nbsp;
This is the most loser of loser politics.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.160
But Republicans and Democrats are nowhere&nbsp;
near the same on this. Let's get this signed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:58.560
Let's get money to the people. Let's move on&nbsp;
to the 15 dollar minimum wage and health care&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.560 --> 00:08:03.760
and vaccine distribution and starting&nbsp;
to open things up as cases and deaths&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.760 --> 00:08:07.760
come down significantly more, hopefully&nbsp;
over the next two to three months

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.160
and all of the other things&nbsp;
that need our attention.

